---
import { url } from '@/lib/url';
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — LabelsCrop';
const description = 'How LabelsCrop handles your data: what never leaves your browser, and what our ad and analytics providers see.';
const lastUpdated = 'September 19, 2026';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
		<h1 data-reveal class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p data-reveal class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

		<div data-reveal class="prose prose-neutral mt-8 max-w-none text-muted-foreground dark:prose-invert">
			<h2>Your files</h2>
			<p>
				LabelsCrop does not have a server that receives, stores, or processes the files you add.
				This covers both kinds of file the site works with: the label PDFs you open in the label
				cropper, and the marketplace payment spreadsheets you open in the profit calculator. All
				cropping, sorting, text extraction, spreadsheet parsing, profit calculation, and file
				generation happen locally in your browser. Your customers' names, addresses and order
				details, and every settlement figure in your payment file, are never transmitted to
				LabelsCrop or any third party by these tools.
			</p>

			<h2>Local storage</h2>
			<p>
				LabelsCrop may save your last-used settings in your browser's local storage so you don't
				have to re-enter them on your next visit. In the label cropper that is things like
				printer size and sort order. In the profit calculator it is the figures you type in
				yourself — your per-SKU making and packing costs, your monthly business expenses, and
				your return write-off rates — so that next month's payment file reuses them.
			</p>
			<p>
				All of it stays on your device, is never transmitted anywhere, and can be cleared at any
				time through your browser settings. Because clearing your browser data also clears it
				permanently, and some browsers expire it on their own after a period of not visiting, the
				profit calculator offers you a spreadsheet backup of your costs that you can keep and
				import again later.
			</p>

			<h2>Advertising</h2>
			<p>
				LabelsCrop is free to use and is supported by advertising, served through Google AdSense.
				Google and its advertising partners may use cookies or similar technologies to serve ads
				based on your prior visits to this or other websites. You can learn more about how Google
				uses this data and manage your ad personalization settings at
				<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
					policies.google.com/technologies/ads
				</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>Analytics</h2>
			<p>
				LabelsCrop uses privacy-friendly, cookie-free analytics to understand aggregate traffic to
				this site (such as which pages are visited). This does not track you individually across
				other websites.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about this policy can be sent to the contact details listed on our
				<a href={url('/about')}>About</a> page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
